  "description": "Illustrative within-host viral-dynamics model.\n\nSource reconciliation 2026-10-20: Illustrative target-cell/virus/immune-response system. The former Ke et al. (2020), Science reference could not be identified as written; its DOI belongs to McKenna et al., a membrane-protein dislocase paper. That unrelated citation is withdrawn, without substituting a different Ke paper as apparent equation evidence. No source supports the specified initial target-cell count, viral inoculum, coefficients or measurement units. The preceding source-only reconciliation preserved equations, initial values, flow topology and layout. Scientific/source fidelity remains unverified.\n\nVersion 1.8 preserves the authored target-cell/virus/immune equations and numeric parameters but explicitly selects Radau on the existing output grid. Immune-mediated infected-cell removal creates a fast timescale; default Euler crosses below zero, whereas independent stiff integration respects the positive continuous dynamics to floating-point tolerance. No unsupported clinical source or SARS-CoV-2 parameter calibration is substituted; source fidelity remains unverified.",
